  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/tiendv89/digital-factory-ui/pulls/43/reviews" \
  -d "{
    \"event\": \"REQUEST_CHANGES\",
    \"body\": $(echo "$REVIEW_BODY" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read()))'),
    \"comments\": [
      {
        \"path\": \"src/features/board/components/KanbanBoard/KanbanBoard.context.tsx\",
        \"line\": 131,
        \"body\": \"🟡 **Important** — Task search sends BOTH `task_id` AND `title` with the same search query.\\n\\nThe backend defines these as independent AND-combined filters over different object fields: `task_id` filters `task_name` (e.g. \\\"T3\\\"), `title` filters the task's title text (e.g. \\\"Workspace search, filters...\\\"). Sending both with the same value means a search for \\\"T3\\\" requires `task_name CONTAINS \\\"T3\\\"` **AND** `title CONTAINS \\\"T3\\\"` — which returns nothing for most tasks.\\n\\n**Fix**: send only `task_id` from the single task-mode search box:\\n\\n```tsx\\ntask_id: boardMode === \\\"task\\\" ? taskSearchQuery : undefined,\\n// remove: title: boardMode === \\\"task\\\" ? taskSearchQuery : undefined\\n```\\n\\nThis was flagged as 🟡 in Cycle 1, the fix removed `task_id` (Cycle 2 caught it missing), and the current fix re-added both — the root cause (two filters from one input) is still unresolved.\"
      }
    ]
  }"
